# Select and persist active players for a new game

Add a six-colour multi-select bar to SCR-000 and persist the chosen active-player set as part of the game.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Red, Blue, White, and Orange are selected by default; Green and Brown are not.
- [x] Tapping a colour toggles its tick immediately and at least one colour must remain selected.
- [x] The control appears above board-size choices and is accessible.
- [x] Starting Standard board stores exactly the selected colours in stable colour order.
- [x] Active players persist across termination; legacy snapshots decode without losing existing players.
- [x] Starting another new game resets the draft selection to the four defaults.
- [x] Domain and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Evidence

- Added a reusable six-colour multi-selector and four-player default on SCR-000.
- Persisted ordered active colours in `BoardSnapshot`, with all-six legacy fallback to preserve existing data.
- Added active-player serialization and default UI coverage.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded.
